{{x}^{2}}{{4}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295041 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "001a0d9f-37c7-5af8-8262-d33442935b95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{64}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292939}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "001a0d9f-37c7-5af8-8262-d33442935b95" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{64}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292939} :answer-field/id #uuid "a0c14e4e-9192-5fc5-bf7f-b01bc1b02f87" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294511}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "79f5cd4e-9f15-597c-8503-3bd19ab1ee0f" :question/math-academy-id "q-279101" :question/problem "![](images/eb/eb9c9b61de232ab6c190a3a324ff3ee2515c61f72a16e2814d77f94a60255501.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=8$ and the vertical radius has length $b=6.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{8}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{6}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{64}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295042 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0845d678-553d-5f9b-8f0c-cc3b9b0a3bcb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{64}+\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{81}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186292966}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id 