{{x}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370998} {:answer/id #uuid "4041e09f-b99a-5bc3-af3a-1a97f34bb588" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370999}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ceeee171-e500-5146-8d03-5a5c1bd03a64" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370998} :answer-field/id #uuid "47ed664f-5269-578c-9dc2-0e5ea600cf72" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370994}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0bf44446-fd59-5eea-85f3-78a8c0b563be" :question/math-academy-id "q-69890" :question/problem "![](images/2a/2a7f7fc248f5582afea5240aa2f7c5f6ee421a53961640efbfae18b9c920c10d.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=4$ and the vertical radius has length $b=3.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{4}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{3}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Wide Ellipse"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087840 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087516 :question/id #uuid "af56117c-65e0-5f12-9780-7a95e6be829e" :question/math-academy-id "e-5072" :question/problem "What is the equation of the ellipse given below?\n\n![](images/3e/3e8d5ed4bf055960b50e046c0688a3c4cc69907ebb1209bb9658ac4bcba48ffe.png)" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x^2}{a^2}+\\dfrac{y^2}{b^2}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=2$ and the vertical radius has length $b=4.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{2}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{4}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "de557d1d-5f27-50e3-bcba-22b21f83267f" :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088122 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "97b2bb68-89cb-59c8-9356-f76f21ec7260" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{81}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293529}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97b2bb68-89cb-59c8-9356-f76f21ec7260" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{81}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293529} :answer-field/id #uuid "0415426c-2704-586e-93d9-ec13672b3656" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293943}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d11d0095-5740-5d82-8a0d-f23a175699b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-279153" :question/problem "![](images/b1/b12eb6672d263655f9f77eaafbf486a7be5bf9b7673c73fd0d75382d192a658b.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=\\frac{3}{2}$ and the vertical radius has length $b=\\frac{9}{2}.$ Therefore, the e