tal radius has length $a=\\frac{5}{2}$ and the vertical radius has length $b=\\frac{7}{2}.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{(\\frac{5}{2})}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{(\\frac{7}{2})}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(\\frac{25}{4})}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{(\\frac{49}{4})} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{4{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{49} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186370017 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "9d1f7bc7-0cdd-5b27-8fe9-02b806603eb7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4{x}^{2}}{49}+\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{121}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370019}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9d1f7bc7-0cdd-5b27-8fe9-02b806603eb7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4{x}^{2}}{49}+\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{121}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370019} :answer-field/id #uuid "357e7c5e-4b53-50fa-852d-a2a0c73a078a" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186370018}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "11b50d3f-8a2a-53bd-9460-027070f70e56" :question/math-academy-id "q-279155" :question/problem "![](images/9d/9deebb67265aafd4fd2c3e7451dddc837c928242ac016a0632907816defcdec1.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?\n\n{{field-1}}$=1$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=\\frac{7}{2}$ and the vertical radius has length $b=\\frac{11}{2}.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{(\\frac{7}{2})}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{(\\frac{11}{2})}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(\\frac{49}{4})}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{(\\frac{121}{4})} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{4{x}^{2}}{49}+\\frac{4{y}^{2}}{121} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186421556 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3c37fde0-293d-5fff-8b41-8792f1c3b2d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{49}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421550} {:answer/id #uuid "60162dda-59fc-569f-9bbc-f89a1da9b64e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{16}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{49}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421551} {:answer/id #uuid "650d25a5-3c4b-5948-9c9f-4ca92962040c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{5}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{7}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421552} {:answer/id #uuid "7a4b634a-7190-518b-8a3e-0e64b953f99a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{49}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421553} {:answer/id #uuid "f7ee88ea-070f-5d68-aaa9-8fb89bd88756" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{7}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{5}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421554}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "3c37fde0-293d-5fff-8b41-8792f1c3b2d4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{49}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421550} :answer-field/id #uuid "a872ab99-4b04-549f-a3e0-8010a8cc8418" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186421555}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "05225557-6476-5115-9d07-1e8467a995db" :question/math-academy-id "q-73631" :question/problem "![](images/39/3989e71a908c5536d97732e253effe16fadb6382a90610db0a8693eec8161393.png)\n\nWhat is the equation of the ellipse given above?" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nHere, the horizontal radius has length $a=5$ and the vertical radius has length $b=7.$ Therefore, the equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{5}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{7}^{2}} & =1 \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{49} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Equation of a Tall Ellipse"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087841 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087517 :question/id #uuid "b7c94673-f847-5977-9b9f-8d235ea42eb2" :question/math-academy-id "e-5073" :question/problem "What are the lengths of the major and minor axes of an ellipse with equation $\\dfrac{x^2}{36} + \\dfrac{y^2}{25} = 1?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x^2}{a^2}+\\dfrac{y^2}{b^2}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have $a^2=36$ and $b^2=25.$\n\n- Since $a^2=36,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{36} = 6.$\n\n- Since $b^2=25,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{25} = 5.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $a=6,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=5.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a = 2 \\cdot 6 = 12,$ and the minor axis has length $2b = 2 \\cdot 5 =10.$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "4e43e393-8752-58bc-b87c-b72f679cbfd9" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186049923 :topic/math-academy-id 1927 :topic/title "The Product Rule for Radicals"}] :knowledge-point/questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186088321 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3b14229b-7244-5a13-b9f7-377caf1b3763" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6$ and $2$" :db/id 