ore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 2=4,$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot \\sqrt{2}=2\\sqrt{2}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186284508 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "01ea4dfa-3746-512d-a4e5-fa19281f7cfe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4\\sqrt{3}$ and $\\sqrt{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281707} {:answer/id #uuid "119639f4-439c-5028-9a09-08e66ef5732b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$2\\sqrt{3}$ and $\\sqrt{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186281856} {:answer/id #uuid "376b6ab6-79ed-53f0-aaa3-87bd75aa6c79" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$12$ and $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282182} {:answer/id #uuid "66196dd8-4f71-57e1-8517-24340f5f07aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4\\sqrt{3}$ and $2\\sqrt{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282569} {:answer/id #uuid "95c0623c-a78b-5fec-8c1e-678b85527dbb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$6$ and $3$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282981}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "66196dd8-4f71-57e1-8517-24340f5f07aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$4\\sqrt{3}$ and $2\\sqrt{3}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186282569} :answer-field/id #uuid "29260e1c-0c08-5549-8699-d160c488888a" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186284008}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2a341dec-953c-5c37-b7a1-a5cd95c6de7d" :question/math-academy-id "q-16454" :question/problem "What are the lengths of the major and minor axes of an ellipse with equation \n$\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{12}=1?$" :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=3$ and ${b}^{2}=12.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=3,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{3}.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=12,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{12}=2\\sqrt{3}.$\n\nSo the semi-major axis has length $b=2\\sqrt{3},$ and the semi-minor axis has length $a=\\sqrt{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 2\\sqrt{3}=4\\sqrt{3},$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot \\sqrt{3}=2\\sqrt{3}.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186294936 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "177cbba2-b79a-5f5d-9c48-f99cc18456dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293025}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "177cbba2-b79a-5f5d-9c48-f99cc18456dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "18" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293025} :answer-field/id #uuid "1b444896-e044-5921-b7f7-0da6232a651c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294016} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "89cbf232-7d5e-5370-98f0-434b0ca4424c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293468}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "89cbf232-7d5e-5370-98f0-434b0ca4424c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293468} :answer-field/id #uuid "643cdb73-3055-524d-9fe7-30a337996809" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294284}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5b7e4e8f-cd81-5ee3-ac55-a56d0433ac6d" :question/math-academy-id "q-277923" :question/problem "For the ellipse \n$\\frac{{x}^{2}}{64}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{81}=1,$ find the lengths of its major and minor axes.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the minor axis is \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=64$ and ${b}^{2}=81.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=64,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{64}=8.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=81,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{81}=9.$\n\nThus, the semi-major axis has length $b=9,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $a=8.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 9=18,$ and the minor axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 8=16.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295047 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6dc25ece-e5e8-5341-b369-60c89d7b7cf0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293391}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6dc25ece-e5e8-5341-b369-60c89d7b7cf0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293391} :answer-field/id #uuid "4b5ea0c3-f3db-587a-a55c-d246902036fa" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294196} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8edd52d8-a856-5699-9135-823330f651e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293486}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8edd52d8-a856-5699-9135-823330f651e5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293486} :answer-field/id #uuid "f2a02e34-a1c4-5302-b6ca-ab014cebd574" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294782}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "26bde4a4-e1ca-5778-ae0f-4fa44e3f19d1" :question/math-academy-id "q-279165" :question/problem "For the ellipse $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1,$ find the lengths of its major and minor axes.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the minor axis is \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=9$ and ${b}^{2}=4.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=9,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{9}=3.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=4,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{4}=2.$\n\nThus, the semi-major axis has length $a=3,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=2.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 3=6,$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 2=4.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295048 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8c243753-ebfb-5bd5-b708-979771972883" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293476}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8c243753-ebfb-5bd5-b708-979771972883" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "12" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293476} :answer-field/id #uuid "2813c84a-d103-5cb1-bd59-405c9d238f89" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294058} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "e23f6045-b753-590b-95e0-5f04f82ba4e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293819}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e23f6045-b753-590b-95e0-5f04f82ba4e9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293819} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f5d06e6-62e7-51fd-886c-846c8398c0d0" :answer-field/key "field-2" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294321}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "05eafcf1-2e1f-53c8-892c-751fcabef6c1" :question/math-academy-id "q-279166" :question/problem "For the ellipse $\\frac{{x}^{2}}{36}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}=1,$ find the lengths of its major and minor axes.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the major axis is \n{{field-1}}.\n\n$\\,$ The length of the minor axis is \n{{field-2}}." :question/worked-solution "Remember that the equation of an ellipse centered at the origin with a horizontal radius of length $a$ and a vertical radius of length $b$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{{a}^{2}}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\n \n\nIn the given equation, we have ${a}^{2}=36$ and ${b}^{2}=16.$\n\n- Since ${a}^{2}=36,$ the length of the horizontal radius must be $a=\\sqrt{36}=6.$\n\n- Since ${b}^{2}=16,$ the length of the vertical radius must be $b=\\sqrt{16}=4.$\n\nThus, the semi-major axis has length $a=6,$ and the semi-minor axis has length $b=4.$\n\nTherefore, the major axis has length $2a=2\\cdot 6=12,$ and the minor axis has length $2b=2\\cdot 4=8.$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186295049 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ee64a24f-4e3c-5796-94b8-769faa4d203e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293859}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ee64a24f-4e3c-5796-94b8-769faa4d203e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "10" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293859} :answer-field/id #uuid "4d433ad7-9ca0-5240-8e86-ff3b484b7323" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186294199} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "c1efda85-532c-5456-9085-146b731f4efb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293689}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c1efda85-532c-5456-9085-146b731f4efb" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186293689} :answer-field/id #uuid "eb9daf9a-554c-59f2-8703-ec452d9cbc